{
	"name": "Animated Shadow",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/creatures/magical/humanoid-silhouette-glowing-pink.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>As an action, your shadow may split away and move independently from you. This shadow acts on your turn, has a movement speed of 30 feet, claws that count as natural weapons, and has a number of hit points equal to 10 + your proficiency bonus. Its AC is 10.</p><p>The shadow acts on your initiative and has one attack, and any attacks that it makes uses your attack bonus (Strength or Dexterity, whichever is higher). On a hit, it deals 2d6 necrotic damage to the target. You may issue a command to your shadow or reattach your shadow to you as a bonus action. If you do not issue a command to your shadow on your turn, it merely defends itself. If your shadow dies, it immediately reattaches itself to you. Once you have used this ability, you cannot use it again until you complete a long rest. </p>",
